            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cardio-MRT provides complex diagnostic information (morphology, function, biochemistry) with little stress for the patient and is therefore used increasingly for clinical diagnosis. There is great need for interdisciplinary studies concerning function, the use of contrast media and spectroscopy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
